A drained share waits on the run queue all the same.
It takes turns before the shares on spare time, and one held to its budget is not;
a share with a ready thread waits on the queue its account and flags say.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a share waits on another queue than its account says

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -181,7 +181,7 @@ static struct share **share_queue(const struct share *s)
     if (!s->drained) {
         return &run_queue;
     }
-    return (s->flags & SHARE_SPARE) ? &spare_queue : &spent_queue;
+    return &run_queue;
 }
 
